# Target exclusions for the `static` gate in .forgejo/workflows/ci.yml.
#
# THIS FILE REPLACES semgrep's built-in list rather than adding to it. Measured
# on 1.178.0: a five-file fixture where the built-in list skipped three went to
# four scanned once a .semgrepignore holding ONE unrelated pattern existed. So
# every directory that should stay out has to be named here, and deleting a line
# below puts that directory back in scope rather than restoring a default.
#
# THE POINT OF THE FILE IS THE TWO LINES THAT ARE NOT IN IT: `tests/` and
# `test/`. bjorn/polybjorn-en#130 measured the gate scanning 25 of 52 tracked
# .js/.mjs/.ts files, and the 27 it missed were the whole test suite, out
# because of the built-in list rather than because anyone decided that. Cost of
# bringing them in, measured with the real p/javascript and p/typescript before
# this was written: 0 findings.
#
# The rest is the built-in list as probed on 1.178.0 rather than read off the
# docs. `__tests__/`, `spec/`, `specs/`, `testing/`, `coverage/`, `out/`,
# `target/`, `third_party/`, `bower_components/`, `.next/`, `.nuxt/`, `.cache/`
# and `env/` are NOT in it, and neither is any `*.test.*` or `*_test.*` FILE
# pattern - which is why lifting two directory lines is the whole change.
node_modules/
vendor/
dist/
build/
.venv/
.tox/
.npm/
*.min.js
